  "thumbnail": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1505740420928-5e560c06d30e?q=80&w=1200&auto=format&fit=crop",
  "keyPoints": {
    "en": [
      "PERFECT timing requires hitting notes within 40ms of the beat—on mobile, screen lag compensation (setting a negative or positive offset in settings) is essential; calibrate using the in-game calibration tool before playing ranked content.",
      "Cards in Project SEKAI have Unit-specific bonus rates—cards from the same Unit (Leo/need, MORE MORE JUMP!, etc.) as the song's featured Unit provide higher Area Item bonus stacking.",
      "The Fever Break system doubles score for notes hit during a Fever state—trigger Fever by hitting notes consecutively without missing; entering Fever on a dense note section provides the highest score multiplier per note.",
      "Event points are earned primarily from playing event songs with event bonus cards—build a team with all 5 event bonus cards (each provides +20% bonus) to reach the maximum 200% event bonus for point efficiency.",
      "Challenge Live (single-song ranked challenge) provides seasonal Stamps for cosmetics and ranking rewards—practise the Challenge Live song in normal mode 3+ times before submitting a score to maximise accuracy in the actual ranked attempt."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "PERFECTタイミングはビートの40ms以内にノートを叩く必要がある。モバイルでは、画面遅延補正（設定でネガティブまたはポジティブオフセットを設定）が必須。ランクコンテンツをプレイする前にゲーム内の校正ツールを使って校正する。",
      "プロジェクトセカイのカードはユニット固有のボーナス率を持つ。楽曲のフィーチャーユニット（Leo/need、MORE MORE JUMP!等）と同じユニットのカードはより高いエリアアイテムボーナスの積み重ねを提供する。",
      "フィーバーブレークシステムはフィーバー状態でのノートのスコアを2倍にする。ミスなしで連続してノートを叩くことでフィーバーをトリガー。密なノートセクションでフィーバーに入ると、ノートごとの最高スコア乗数を提供する。",
      "イベントポイントは主にイベントボーナスカードでイベント曲をプレイすることで獲得される。最大200%のイベントボーナスを達成するために5枚全てのイベントボーナスカード（それぞれ+20%ボーナスを提供）でチームを構築する。",
      "チャレンジライブ（シングルソングランクチャレンジ）はコスメティックのための季節スタンプとランキング報酬を提供する。実際のランク挑戦の精度を最大化するために、スコアを送信する前にチャレンジライブの楽曲を通常モードで3回以上練習する。"
    ]
  },
  "opening": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Difficulty Progression Path",
        "body": "Project SEKAI has four difficulty levels: EASY, NORMAL, HARD, and MASTER. Begin on HARD for songs you can achieve 80%+ PERFECT on—HARD provides higher score than EASY/NORMAL while being accessible to intermediate rhythm game players. Move to MASTER only when HARD consistently produces Full Combo (no missed notes) performance. MASTER notes include simultaneous holds and slide notes that require different finger placements than HARD, necessitating pattern-specific practice sessions."
      },
      {
        "title": "Card Skill Activation",
        "body": "Card Skills in Project SEKAI activate during the song at fixed intervals—Score Boost skills (SB) increase the score of notes hit during the activation window. Stack Score Boost skills from all 5 team members to create overlapping windows where all 5 skills are simultaneously active. The optimal team has 5 Score Boost skills with staggered timing so at least 2 are always active throughout the song rather than all 5 activating simultaneously during one dense section."
      }
    ]
  },
  "midGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Master Pass and 3DMV Content",
        "body": "Event stories and Virtual Lives (virtual concerts) provide the primary non-gacha Crystals income. Virtual Lives require purchasing Show Tickets—earn tickets through event participation and daily missions. Each Virtual Live provides 50 Crystals per attendance. Event stories provide 10 Crystals per chapter on first completion. Completing all event stories and attending all Virtual Lives consistently provides enough Crystals for 1 guaranteed pull per month without spending."
      },
      {
        "title": "Co-op and Cheerful Carnival Events",
        "body": "Cheerful Carnival events are limited competitive events where two teams (opposing sides) earn points for their team. The winning team member with the highest personal contribution earns exclusive reward titles. To maximise contribution: play on the highest difficulty with maximum event bonus cards, use Energy Drinks (stamina items) during the final 48 hours when team point thresholds matter most, and activate Show Items (multi-player boosters) during cooperative live sessions."
      }
    ]
  },
  "endGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "MASTER FC and AP Goals",
        "body": "Full Combo (FC, no missed notes) and All Perfect (AP, all notes PERFECT or GREAT) on MASTER are the primary skill milestones. FC requires pattern memorisation and consistent timing—practice sessions of 30+ plays on a single song before attempting FC are standard at the MASTER level. AP requires near-zero timing errors across the entire song; use the Perfect Rate stat to identify which note sections have the highest error rate and focus practise specifically on those 2–3 bar segments."
      }
    ]
  },
  "mistakes": {
    "en": [
      "Not calibrating audio and visual offset—Project SEKAI has separate audio and visual offset calibration; an uncalibrated device will consistently produce GREAT instead of PERFECT results regardless of player skill.",
      "Building event teams with maximum rarity instead of maximum event bonus—event bonus percentage is more valuable than card strength for event point farming; a lower-rarity event bonus card contributes more event points than a non-event SSR.",
      "Spending Crystals on non-banner-limited pulls—standard gachas in Project SEKAI have the same SSR rate throughout the year; limited event banners (higher feature rates for event-specific SSRs) are the highest-value Crystal spending.",
      "Not using natural stamina regeneration efficiently—stamina regenerates over time; setting a reminder to play at maximum stamina capacity ensures no regeneration is wasted.",
      "Skipping event ranking rewards—top event ranking provides exclusive card borders and titles unavailable elsewhere; participating in the final 24-hour sprint (highest point multiplier window) is the most efficient ranking investment."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "オーディオとビジュアルのオフセットを校正しない。プロジェクトセカイには個別のオーディオとビジュアルオフセット校正がある。未校正のデバイスはプレイヤースキルに関わらず一貫してPERFECTの代わりにGREATを生成する。",
      "イベントボーナスの最大化ではなく最高レアリティでイベントチームを構築する。イベントポイントファーミングではイベントボーナスパーセンテージはカードの強さより価値が高い。低レアリティのイベントボーナスカードは非イベントSSRよりも多くのイベントポイントに貢献する。",
      "バナー限定ではない引きにクリスタルを使う。プロジェクトセカイの標準ガチャは年間を通じて同じSSR率を持つ。限定イベントバナー（イベント固有SSRの高いフィーチャー率）が最高価値のクリスタルの使い道。",
      "スタミナの自然回復を効率的に使わない。スタミナは時間をかけて回復する。最大スタミナ容量でプレイするリマインダーを設定することで回復の無駄がなくなる。",
      "イベントランキング報酬をスキップする。トップイベントランキングは他では入手できない独占カードボーダーとタイトルを提供する。最終24時間のスプリント（最高ポイント乗数ウィンドウ）に参加することが最も効率的なランキング投資。"
    ]
  },
